---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Her Majesty's Displeasure - wReady Showcase" description="A dark political satire about MI5, The Beatles, and institutional absurdity">
  <article class="project-detail">
    
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="project-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/wready">wReady</a> / <a href="/wready/projects">Projects</a> / Her Majesty's Displeasure
        </div>
        <h1><em>Her Majesty's Displeasure</em></h1>
        <p class="project-meta">Television · Limited Series · 6 Episodes</p>
        <p class="logline">
          When The Beatles are awarded MBEs in 1965, Prince Philip responds not with pride but by 
          quietly unleashing MI5 to rein them in. Caught between royal paranoia and John Lennon's 
          growing rebellion, two hapless intelligence officers oversee a campaign that exposes how 
          petty grudges, bad paperwork, and institutional absurdity can reshape history.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Series Bible -->
    <section class="bible-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Series Bible</h2>
        
        <div class="bible-grid">
          
          <div class="bible-card">
            <h3>Tone</h3>
            <p>
              Dark, cynical, and greatly satirical, with key focuses on the power dynamics between 
              the royal family and the Beatles and on the absurdity of the royal institutions, the 
              characters, and the situations they find themselves in. Historically accurate regarding 
              actual events and dates when possible, but takes liberties to create a more dramatic 
              and engaging story.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bible-card">
            <h3>Visual Language</h3>
            <p><strong>The Royal/MI5 World:</strong> Rigid symmetry, desaturated color palettes 
            (greys, muted blues, pale yellows), meticulously ordered but dusty production design. 
            Deadpan, flat, wide framing emphasizing sterile absurdity.</p>
            <p><strong>The Beatles' World:</strong> Chaotic, warmer, organic. Handheld or fluid 
            camera movements during creative sessions. Cluttered with instruments, art, and life.</p>
            <p><strong>Visual Irony:</strong> Comedy from chaotic elements (Yoko's art, clumsy spies) 
            introduced into rigidly composed Royal frames.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bible-card">
            <h3>Central Dramatic Question</h3>
            <p>
              Can an individual artist's authentic, chaotic rebellion survive a confrontation with 
              the soulless, absurd machinery of the state, or will both be transformed by the encounter?
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bible-card">
            <h3>Setting</h3>
            <p>
              Primary narrative spans 1965 to 1970. Begins in London with The Beatles receiving their 
              MBEs, follows a covert multi-year campaign, and culminates in a failed assassination 
              attempt in 1970. Epilogue in mid-1970s shows characters settled into their lives.
            </p>
            <p class="closing-note">
              <em>Concludes with title card: "John Lennon was assassinated by Mark David Chapman on 
              December 8, 1980. There is no evidence that the royal family had any involvement."</em>
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Comparisons -->
    <section class="comps-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Tonal & Structural Comparisons</h2>
        <div class="comps-grid">
          
          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>Patriot <span class="creator">(Steven Conrad)</span></h3>
            <p>Deadpan humor, bureaucratic melancholy, and the depiction of intelligence work as a soul-crushing office job.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>The Royal Tenenbaums <span class="creator">(Wes Anderson)</span></h3>
            <p>Portrayal of a dysfunctional, iconic family, specific visual aesthetic, and blend of comedy with genuine pathos.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>The Death of Stalin <span class="creator">(Armando Iannucci)</span></h3>
            <p>Sharp, satirical take on a powerful institution in crisis and depiction of powerful figures as petty, incompetent, and self-serving.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>Breaking Bad / Better Call Saul <span class="creator">(Vince Gilligan)</span></h3>
            <p>Restrained camera direction to withhold and reveal consequence. Institutional harm as a series of reasonable decisions that accumulate into irreversible damage.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Themes -->
    <section class="themes-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Core Themes</h2>
        <div class="themes-grid">
          
          <div class="theme-card">
            <h3>Power vs. Art</h3>
            <p>The central conflict between the rigid, inherited power of the state and the chaotic, earned influence of a creative individual. Does true art always threaten established power?</p>
          </div>

          <div class="theme-card">
            <h3>Absurdity of Bureaucracy</h3>
            <p>How institutional processes and paperwork can transform human decisions into mechanical cruelty, with no single person feeling responsible.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="theme-card">
            <h3>Myth vs. Reality</h3>
            <p>The gap between public personas and private truths, both for The Beatles and the Royal Family. How legends are constructed and maintained.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="theme-card">
            <h3>Nature of Rebellion</h3>
            <p>What makes rebellion authentic versus performative? Can institutional power co-opt or neutralize genuine dissent?</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sample Locations -->
    <section class="locations-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Key Locations</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          The series moves between the sterile world of MI5 and Buckingham Palace and the creative 
          chaos of The Beatles' recording spaces.
        </p>
        
        <div class="locations-grid">
          
          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>Abbey Road Studios</h3>
            <span class="location-type">INT</span>
            <p>Legendary London recording studio, filled with musical history. Creative, tense, iconic atmosphere with posters, scattered instruments, and sunlight through frosted glass.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>Apple Studios</h3>
            <span class="location-type">INT</span>
            <p>The Beatles' own recording space in their Apple Corps headquarters. More intimate and experimental than Abbey Road, reflecting their growing independence.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>Apple Studios Rooftop</h3>
            <span class="location-type">EXT</span>
            <p>Site of the famous rooftop concert. Cold, windy, with London skyline visible. The final public performance of The Beatles.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>MI5 Offices</h3>
            <span class="location-type">INT</span>
            <p>Drab, fluorescent-lit government offices. Beige walls, filing cabinets, typewriters. The mundane machinery of state surveillance.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>Buckingham Palace</h3>
            <span class="location-type">INT</span>
            <p>Ornate but cold. Gilded frames, heavy curtains, portraits of ancestors. The weight of tradition and inherited power.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="location-card">
            <h3>Brian Epstein's Office</h3>
            <span class="location-type">INT</span>
            <p>Stylish but increasingly cluttered. Beatles memorabilia, contracts, photographs. The business side of the band's empire.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technical Features -->
    <section class="technical-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>wReady Implementation</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          This project showcases wReady's full screenplay management capabilities:
        </p>
        
        <div class="features-grid">
          
          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📝 Screenplay Formatting</h3>
            <p>Custom MDX plugin for industry-standard screenplay formatting with scene headings, action lines, dialogue, and transitions.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>🎭 Character Database</h3>
            <p>Detailed profiles for John Lennon, Paul McCartney, Prince Philip, MI5 agents, and supporting characters with arcs and relationships.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📍 Location Library</h3>
            <p>Organized database of all filming locations with INT/EXT designation, mood notes, and scene associations.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📊 Plot Threading</h3>
            <p>Main and sub-plots tracked across all six episodes with beat-by-beat breakdowns and tension analysis.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>🎨 Thematic Analysis</h3>
            <p>Four core themes connected across scenes and episodes to maintain narrative coherence and depth.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📈 Tension Graphing</h3>
            <p>Visual representation of dramatic tension across episodes to ensure proper pacing and structure.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <h2>Interested in the Full Series Bible?</h2>
          <p>
            This showcase provides an overview of the project. The complete series bible includes 
            detailed episode breakdowns, character arcs, scene-by-scene analysis, and full screenplay 
            formatting examples.
          </p>
          <a href="/wready/projects" class="cta-button">← Back to Projects</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-detail {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .project-hero {
    padding: 3rem 0 4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .project-meta {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .logline {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  /* Sections */
  .bible-section,
  .comps-section,
  .themes-section,
  .locations-section,
  .technical-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .comps-section,
  .technical-section {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }

  .section-intro {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Bible Grid */
  .bible-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .bible-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .bible-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .bible-card p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .bible-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .bible-card strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .closing-note {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  /* Comps Grid */
  .comps-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .comp-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .comp-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .creator {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: normal;
  }

  .comp-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Themes Grid */
  .themes-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .theme-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .theme-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .theme-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Locations Grid */
  .locations-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .location-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .location-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .location-type {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .location-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Features Grid */
  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .feature-item h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .feature-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* CTA Section */
  .cta-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .cta-box {
    padding: 3rem;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-box h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .cta-box p {
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: all var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    background: var(--accent-dark);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    }

    .comps-grid,
    .themes-grid,
    .locations-grid,
    .features-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cta-box {
      padding: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>